## SECTION 2: ALL BUILT-IN MONGODB ROLES

### 📁 Single-Database Roles
* **`read`**
  Allows a user to read data (run queries, find documents) on all non-system collections.
* **`readWrite`**
  Provides full data modification rights. Users can insert, update, or delete documents on all non-system collections.

### 🗄️ Database Administration Roles
* **`dbAdmin`**
  Allows structural administration tasks within the specific database. A user with this role can create collections, drop collections, manage indexes, run the profiler, and generate execution plans. *Security Restriction: They are strictly not allowed to modify collection document data itself.*
* **`userAdmin`**
  Grants the ability to create, update, delete, and manage users and custom roles on that specific database. 
  *🔒 Security Warning: Because a `userAdmin` can grant any rights (including their own) to other users, they are indirectly a `dbOwner`. If a user gets `userAdmin` rights on the global `admin` database, they can assign themselves to the `root` role to become a complete system superuser.*
* **`dbOwner`**
  The absolute master of the local database. Combines the full permissions of `readWrite`, `dbAdmin`, and `userAdmin` into a single container role.

### 🌐 Any-Database Roles (Apply across the whole instance)
* **`readAnyDatabase`**
  Grants `read` permissions across all databases on the server (except `local` and `config`).
* **`readWriteAnyDatabase`**
  Grants `readWrite` permissions across all databases on the server (except `local` and `config`).
* **`dbAdminAnyDatabase`**
  Grants `dbAdmin` administrative permissions across all databases on the server.
* **`userAdminAnyDatabase`**
  Grants `userAdmin` credentials management across all databases on the server.

### ⚙️ Cluster Administration Roles
* **`clusterAdmin`**
  The highest administrative role for cluster operations. Combines `clusterManager`, `clusterMonitor`, and `hostManager`.
* **`clusterManager`**
  Allows sharding management, replica set actions, and deployment maintenance.
* **`clusterMonitor`**
  Provides read-only access to server monitoring metrics, `db.serverStatus()`, and monitoring tools.
* **`hostManager`**
  Allows monitoring and managing the server host machine (shutting down services, checking metrics).

### 💾 Backup & Restore Roles
* **`backup`**
  Grants the minimal necessary privileges to back up data using tools like `mongodump`.
* **`restore`**
  Grants the privileges to restore data using tools like `mongorestore` (excluding system settings).

### 👑 Superuser Role
* **`root`**
  Complete access to everything. Combines all "Any-Database" roles, cluster administration roles, backup/restore roles, and direct system manipulation rights.

