## SECTION 3: CUSTOM SECURITY ROLE TEMPLATES

### 🛠️ Template A: Custom Database Administrator ("DBA")
**Scope:** Single Target Database (`LAB`).
**Permissions:** Inherits basic `read` data capabilities, but restricts schema updates strictly to document insertions, modifications, index building, and collection provisioning across all collections in the target database.
```javascript
use LAB

db.createRole({
  createRole: "DBA",
  privileges: [
    { 
      resource: { db: "LAB", collection: "" },
      actions: [ "insert", "update", "createIndex", "createCollection" ] 
    }
  ],
  roles: [
    { role: "read", db: "LAB" }
  ]
})
```

### 🛠️ Template B: Instance-Wide Broad Data Writer ("Mongodb")
**Scope:** Universal Server Scope (All Databases).
**Permissions:** Inherits instance-wide default query reading (`readAnyDatabase` via `admin`), while adding specific granular permissions to write records and generate performance indexes across all structural layers.
```javascript
use admin

db.createRole({
  createRole: "Mongodb",
  privileges: [
    { 
      resource: { db: "", collection: "" },
      actions: [ "insert", "update", "createIndex" ] 
    }
  ],
  roles: [
    { role: "readAnyDatabase", db: "admin" }
  ]
})
```

### 🛠️ Template C: Instance-Wide Complete Global Writer ("DBA1")
**Scope:** Universal Server Scope (All Databases).
**Permissions:** Implements a direct global wrapper role giving comprehensive read and write modification properties across all database layers on the cluster instance.
```javascript
use admin

db.createRole({
  createRole: "DBA1",
  privileges: [],
  roles: [
    { role: "readWriteAnyDatabase", db: "admin" }
  ]
})
```
